# AGENTS.md — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

> Router. This file holds only the rules that apply to every task and a map of
> where the rest lives. Open the owner doc a task needs, and nothing more.

## Hard rules (worth interrupting a change over)

<!-- The handful the team most wants enforced. Irreversible actions (direct data
     writes, money, outbound email, production) belong here first. Examples —
     keep the project's real ones: -->
- Descriptive names always; in `map`/`filter`/etc. use the singular. Rename
  cryptic identifiers in code you touch. ({{NAMING_STRICTNESS}})
- Never compare against a string literal where a domain enum exists; never show
  a raw enum key to a user — translate via {{LABEL_MAP_LOCATION}}.
- Never reach past the repository layer; never expose a persistence entity —
  map to a DTO.
- Concurrent writes go in a transaction; critical operations
  ({{CRITICAL_OPS}}) are idempotent.
- Never swallow an error; log with context and propagate or return typed.
- Every lookup by a client-supplied ID is scoped to the caller ({{AUTHZ_CHECK}});
  the tenant/user comes from the session, never the request.
- New dependency, skill or plugin versions wait {{QUARANTINE_DAYS}} days after
  release before we adopt them; a security-fix bypass is explicit and recorded.
- Input never becomes code: parameterized queries only, commands take an args
  array, no raw HTML from users.
{{ENTRY_FILE_LOCK}}  <!-- e.g. "- Never edit this file without {{OWNER}}'s explicit approval; propose the change and wait." Only if chosen at init. -->

